<title>POLAND: POLL-POLISH BANKS SEE END-97 CPI AT 14.50 PCT.</title>
<headline>POLL-POLISH BANKS SEE END-97 CPI AT 14.50 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inflation expectations among Polish banks rose for the first time in three months in August, a monthly Reuter poll of the 27 biggest banks showed on Monday.</p>
<p>The average of predicted year-on-year inflation for the end of 1997 was 14.50 percent, up from 13.76 percent predicted last month and above the government's goal of 13 percent.</p>
<p>The average August inflation forecast was 0.67 percent.</p>
<p>		  AUGUST	 END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> CPI AVERAGE   0.67	14.50 (13.76)     12.92 (12.18)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   0.00	13.40 (12.30)     10.80 (10.00)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   1.65	16.00 (16.00)     16.50 (14.00)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and July-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
